# Worktrees live inside the repo for convenience; git must never stage one.
# A shell cwd reset plus `git add -A` in the MAIN checkout committed an entire
# worktree as an embedded repo on 2026-08-26 (seventh stray-write incident, and
# the first that could have destroyed work: undoing it with --hard would have
# deleted the worktree the commit had swallowed). The SDLC rule said "use
# absolute paths"; the rule was written and then broken by its own author the
# next day. This line is the mechanical version of it.
.claude/worktrees/

# Forensics written by app/scripts/test-run.sh on a killed run. Local only --
# the SDLC teardown gate checks `git status` on the main checkout, so an
# un-ignored capture directory would trip it on the first real memory kill.
app/.test-kills/
